ve at the end—or perhaps as Bob would say, the beginning. Because this story, like life itself, doesn't truly end. It continues, chapter after chapter, each one building on what came before, each one offering new challenges and new joys, new freedoms and new responsibilities. I've written about the shock that ignited Bobs curiosity, the childhood that shaped his passions, the education that equipped him for the journey, the career that fulfilled his ambitions, the family that gave his life meaning, the travels that expanded his horizons, the losses that taught him what's precious, the love that carried him through.</p>
<p>But the story doesn't stop here.</p>
